package com.marketlabs.pulse.storage.model.stocks

// Generated by Claude Code.

/**
 * 💡 THOUGHT PROCESS:
 * Replaces the old single `StockAnalysis` domain model with two — `StockPreview` and
 * `StockDetail` — mirroring the backend's split of one merged deep-study document into a small
 * always-cached preview and a large detail fetched only on tap (see `NetworkStockPreview.kt` /
 * `NetworkStockDetail.kt` for the backend-side rationale).
 *
 * Every optional field stays genuinely nullable per the project's "null over arbitrary defaults"
 * rule — this AI-enriched payload can legitimately be partially absent, and a `""`/`0` default
 * would be indistinguishable from a real empty/zero value from the backend.
 *
 * Backend enums (`technicalSetup`, `direction`, `category`, `macdSignal`, `rateSensitivity`,
 * `predicate`, `status`, `urgency`, `impactMagnitude`, `regimeAtAnalysis`) are kept as plain
 * `String?` rather than Kotlin enums, same reasoning as the old model: an unrecognized/new
 * backend value shouldn't crash deserialization, and this codebase already has an unrelated
 * `TechnicalSetup` enum (utils/enums/MarketEnums.kt) for the tactical-momentum pillar with a
 * completely different value set — reusing that name here would collide. Classification into
 * colors/labels happens at the UI layer, same as `AssetOverview`'s `macdSignal`/`technicalStatus`.
 */

